From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Use FreeBSD SA_* values for the PS4 raw sigaction call.

The PS4 SDK headers give this translation unit Linux SA_* constants, but the
raw sigaction system call (416) that the native signal path makes is parsed
by the console's FreeBSD-derived kernel, which reads the FreeBSD values.
Redefine SA_ONSTACK, SA_RESTART, SA_RESETHAND, SA_NODEFER and SA_SIGINFO for
__PROSPERO__ in signal_x86_64.c only, matching the measured correction that
orbis-compat/include/signal.h carries for ordinary applications. The host
build and other signal users are unchanged.

This change shipped in the console tree from 01.06 onward (GLDS10043 01.41 =
v0.0.1, 01.43 = v0.0.2) but was never in the patch series; it is recovered
here verbatim from that tree.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -65,6 +65,23 @@
 #ifdef HAVE_SYS_UCONTEXT_H
 # include <sys/ucontext.h>
 #endif
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* The PS4 SDK exposes Linux SA_* constants to this FreeBSD-derived kernel.
+ * Raw sigaction syscall 416 parses the FreeBSD values; orbis-compat/include/
+ * signal.h carries the same measured correction for regular applications.
+ * Keep this translation unit's direct syscall ABI correct without changing
+ * the host Wine build or other signal users. */
+# undef SA_ONSTACK
+# define SA_ONSTACK   0x0001
+# undef SA_RESTART
+# define SA_RESTART   0x0002
+# undef SA_RESETHAND
+# define SA_RESETHAND 0x0004
+# undef SA_NODEFER
+# define SA_NODEFER   0x0010
+# undef SA_SIGINFO
+# define SA_SIGINFO   0x0040
+#endif
 #ifdef __APPLE__
 # include <mach/mach.h>
 /* _thread_set_tsd_base is private API for setting GSBASE, added in macOS 10.12.
-- 
